hi everyone its Johanna here this is a  requested video and I think it's a  really important topic to speak about on  binge eating some of us might be going  through this right now and it's actually  sabotaging our workout plan and we want  to be able to stop binge eating and so I  hope this video will be able to help you  out so what is binge eating binge eating  is characterized as a compulsive  overeating in which you consume huge  amounts of food within a short period of  time when you're binging  you are out of control it's a vicious  cycle you feel depressed and it's just  an angry and so you pinch and then you  feel even more depressed anxious and  angry about binging and so you binge  again so what are the causes of binge  eating the two most common causes are  number one driven by emotion you feel  anxious angry upset and you choose to  use food to suppress your emotions  instead of dealing with it  another reason can be that you are  currently on a starvation diet or you  have previously been on an extreme diet  the issues I have with extreme diets is  that they do not teach lifestyle changes  which can be maintained over the years  hence when you deprive your body from  the nutrition and food your body needs  eventually your body will repel and  overcompensate with the first binge the  binging starts irregularly but over time  it will become more frequent and it will  become a habit according to research 3.5  percent of US women suffer from binge  eating and that is more than double the  amount of bulimia and more than four  times of anorexia binge eating happens  regularly at least twice a week over a  period of six months so ask yourself  these questions number one do you feel  out of control or unable to stop when  you're eating - do you think about food  all the time 3 do you force yourself to  eat even when you're full and  SiC afterwards for do you stock up food  and eat secretly five do you eat excape  your worries stress or to come for  yourself six  do you eat continuously throughout the  day without any set meal times 7 do you  feel disgusted guilty and ashamed of  yourself after eating and finally are  you desperate to take control of your  weight and your eating habits if your  answers I guess to most of these  questions let's take a look at how we  can stop sabotaging our workout plan  with unhealthy binge eating here are my  top ten tips tip number one is to keep  binge at bay so instead of depriving  yourself from your cravings and  indulging to the entire bar of chocolate  over weekends why not have small  portions of these few times a week so  instead of eating directly from the  chocolate bar break them into small  pieces have a couple of small blocks and  stall the rest away this way you are  more in control of your food portion and  you are enjoying your food instead of  feeling guilty afterwards the second tip  is to set yourself a timer wait when you  have the urge to binge stop set yourself  a 15 minutes timer and think do you  actually feel hungry or are you actually  feeling upset stress which make you want  to stuff yourself with all the chocolate  bars if you're feeling upset take the  time to think what's going on or is it  just boredom if it's your emotions then  let's not numb ourselves with food but  take the courage to do with your  emotions don't hide your emotions speak  to someone speak to your friends or your  families we women tend to binge on our  own  instead I want you to pick up the phone  call someone that you're close to your  friends or your family members and share  your emotions I'm sure they will  time to listen to your problems and to  give you some positive advice to make  you feel good or you can even speak to a  professional that will be able to help  you out to do with your issues so stop  using food as your comfort but instead  speak to someone because this will be a  long-term success in avoiding binge  eating on the other hand if you find  yourself going through the fridge  looking for something to eat but you are  not sure what to eat you are most likely  experiencing boredom cravings grab  yourself a glass of water drink your  water and walk away or find another  distraction do whatever you need to do  to get your mind off the craving go out  for a walk go for a job do it an  activity you enjoy my favorite is just  to take the time to relax and clear your  mind listen to some calming music  meditate and just even go for a nap when  you wake up you will feel so much better  and you will not be binge eating so try  that out just listen to calming music  and go for a nap trust me you will feel  better another of my favorite method is  to chew on gums if you really have to  put something into your mouth because of  your cravings or because you're stressed  out chew gums this will reduce your  craving and it will also help you to  reduce your stress level and to calm you  down so if you have to chew gums quite  often in a day I would say try it out  and do it and you will really calm you  down and reduce your cravings the next  step is to record your intelligences  even if you've just eaten an entire  chocolate bar is not too late to do  something about it write down what  triggers you to binge so that you can  overcome it in the  future stop take a step back reflect and  learn to take control of the situation  instead of allowing your emotions and  your food to take control so start  writing down your indulgences the next  tip is something I've always emphasized  on whether you want to lose weight to  maintain your weight or to stop binge  eating which is to start your day right  by having your breakfast research has  shown that those who do not pack their  breakfast are more prone to binge eating  and to have higher calorie meals  throughout the day so start your day  right by having a breakfast you can  watch some of my videos for really quick  and simple breakfast ideas they do not  have to be complicated at all and tip  number eight is please do not ever go on  a restricted diet ever again you have  tried them and they have been proven not  to work in fact you might have even put  on more weight before you started  dieting start educating yourself with  healthy eating look for healthy and  delicious recipes and enjoy your  cravings in moderation this will not  only help you to lose weight but I  guarantee you you will be able to  sustain it for life and my next tip is  to start getting active plan an exercise  program which you will want to maintain  this can be either working out with my  workout videos or join a dance club stay  active does not only make you feel young  look your best it will also keep you  happy and energized but do not punish  yourself in the gym after a binge stick  to your regular workout routine maybe  you can go for an extra walk but avoid  the mindset of working off the calories  you consume this too can lead to an  unhealthy cycle of binge eating and over  exercising so the key here is to do with  a core issue of your binging instead of  working the calories off because it will  not help in long-term and finally learn  to love and forgive yourself stop  beating yourself up over it you did not  stop binging overnight  will not be able to stop that quickly  either every step you take away from  binge eating will make you feel better  about yourself it will take months or  even years to completely change your  habits but start to love yourself for  who you are and not what you look like  just like any other addictions binging  develops into a habit in order to break  this cycle  stop picking up new positive habits and  focus on them the key to success is to  try and try and try again and you will  get there for new fitness food and  motivational videos please like share  and subscribe to my You Tube channel and  website do follow me on Facebook  Instagram and Twitter to stay connected  with me thanks guys  you
 

